WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Dr. Farah Nasser>Okay, lab meeting. First item is the grant renewal, the application is due on December 1.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.000
<v Leo Martins>The preliminary results section still needs the new microscopy figures.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
<v Dr. Farah Nasser>Leo, can you finish those figures by Friday?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
<v Leo Martins>Yes, I'll have them ready by Friday.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:41.000
<v Ines Duarte>One issue: the confocal microscope has been booked solid by the other group, so I can't image the new samples until next month.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:50.000
<v Dr. Farah Nasser>That's a real bottleneck. I'll talk to the facility manager about reserving time for us.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
<v Sam Okoye>Should we include the mouse data in the renewal, or keep it for the paper?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Dr. Farah Nasser>We'll leave the mouse data out of the renewal. It's not replicated yet.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Sam Okoye>Okay. Also, the minus eighty freezer alarm went off twice this week, I'm worried it's failing.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.000
<v Ines Duarte>I can call the service company tomorrow.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Dr. Farah Nasser>Please do. Someone should also move the critical samples to the backup freezer today.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
<v Sam Okoye>I'll do that right after this.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:46.000
<v Leo Martins>Who is going to present at the department seminar next month?

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.000
<v Dr. Farah Nasser>Good question, I haven't decided yet.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:01.000
<v Dr. Farah Nasser>Last thing, we agreed to switch to the new electronic lab notebook starting January.
